{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And in the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, is HaShem's Passover.</b> It does not mention here 'between the evenings,' for it is already well known. And note that it does not mention the Sabbath burnt-offering during the seven days of Passover, just as it does not mention the wave-offering of the omer that is spoken of in the section 'Speak to the priests' (Leviticus 23:7). And it says 'all manner of servile work' (כל מלאכת עבודה) and does not say 'all work' (כל מלאכה) as in the case of the Sabbath, because a festival day is permitted for the preparation of food; and when it mentions elsewhere (Exodus 12:16) 'no manner of work shall be done in them,' it needed to specify (ibid.) 'that which every soul may eat.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:44.542319860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}